# The Ashee composition audit, as a systemd user service.
#
# ## Why this is a timer and not a GitHub workflow
#
# `system-audit.sh` is a *composition* audit. It resolves its root to the parent of its own
# directory and then asks whether the projects it can see are under version control, whether their
# package scripts point outside their repository, and whether their archives sit beside their
# sources. A GitHub runner has cloned exactly one repository, so those questions would be asked about
# the wrong set of directories — it would report a confident subset of the truth, which is worse than
# reporting nothing.
#
# The script has documented its own scheduled mode since it was written:
#
#     CI=1 ./system-audit.sh     # exits 1 on findings, for a scheduled job
#
# This is that job. Nothing else was missing from the script; the scheduler was.
#
# ## Install
#
#     mkdir -p ~/.config/systemd/user ~/.local/state/ashee-audit
#     cp harness/systemd/ashee-system-audit.* ~/.config/systemd/user/
#     systemctl --user daemon-reload
#     systemctl --user enable --now ashee-system-audit.timer
#
# ## Read it, and turn it off
#
#     journalctl --user -u ashee-system-audit -n 80
#     tail ~/.local/state/ashee-audit.log
#     systemctl --user list-timers ashee-system-audit.timer
#     systemctl --user disable --now ashee-system-audit.timer
#
# **A failing unit is the point, not a fault.** `CI=1` makes a finding an exit code, so the audit
# appears in `systemctl --user --failed` instead of in a log somebody has to remember to read. While
# the composition has open findings, this unit will report failed every week. That is the signal
# working; silencing it by dropping `CI=1` would restore exactly the state the check exists to end —
# a report that is always green because it cannot be red.

[Unit]
Description=The Ashee composition audit (harness/system-audit.sh)
Documentation=file:%h/Documents/Ashee-Softworks/my_new_folder/harness/README.md

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=%h/Documents/Ashee-Softworks/my_new_folder
# The mode the script documents for a scheduled job: exits non-zero on findings.
Environment=CI=1
# A report that only exists in a journal is hard to compare week to week, so it is written down.
# Outside every repository on purpose: a timer that dirties a working tree would itself become the
# finding the next run reports.
ExecStartPre=/bin/mkdir -p %h/.local/state/ashee-audit
ExecStart=/bin/sh %h/Documents/Ashee-Softworks/my_new_folder/harness/system-audit.sh
StandardOutput=append:%h/.local/state/ashee-audit/ashee-system-audit.log
StandardError=append:%h/.local/state/ashee-audit/ashee-system-audit.log
